{# ---------- Impact framing ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="container split split--wide-media">
    <div class="flow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
      <h2 id="why-title">A gift here reaches far beyond Austin</h2>
      <p>For more than 30 years the Steve Hicks School of Social Work has sent students to learn alongside practitioners around the world, from the School's first regular international placement with UNHCR in Geneva in 1993 to practicums today in Santiago, Oaxaca, Wellington, Cape Town and with UNHCR in Geneva and Budapest. Students have been placed on every continent except Antarctica.</p>
      <p>Those experiences do not stay abroad. Students return to Texas with cross-cultural skills, new models of practice and a wider sense of what social work can do. Faculty bring back research partners. Communities gain long-term collaborators. That is the ripple effect your gift sets in motion.</p>
      <p>Partner with us to transform lives globally through research, education and practice.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://socialwork.utexas.edu/give/">Give now</a>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/connect/">Talk with us about a gift</a>
        <!-- VERIFY: School giving page URL (socialwork.utexas.edu/give/). -->
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <blockquote class="pullquote">Social workers address society's greatest challenges at home and abroad.</blockquote>
      <figcaption class="pullquote-cite">Noël Busch-Armendariz, Ph.D., Associate Dean for Global Engagement</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- What your gift makes possible ---------- #}
<section class="section section--sand" aria-labelledby="possible-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your impact</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="possible-title">What your gift makes possible</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">Gifts to the Office of Global Engagement are directed where they remove the biggest barriers for students and open the most promising doors for faculty and partners.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-list feature-list--2">
      <li><strong>Student travel and practicum support.</strong> Airfare, housing and living costs are the main reason a qualified student turns down a practicum abroad. Scholarships make the semester possible for students who could not otherwise go.</li>
      <li><strong>Signature programs.</strong> From Texas to the Troubles takes students, faculty and staff from Austin to Dublin and Belfast to study constructive dialogue and leadership in divided societies. Support keeps the cohort accessible.</li>
      <li><strong>Faculty research partnerships.</strong> Collaborations like the clinical master's program with Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile and Cortando la Brecha in Puerto Rico depend on faculty being able to travel, co-teach and co-write with partners.</li>
      <li><strong>Visiting scholars.</strong> Bringing partner faculty to Austin, as Tallinn University's Erasmus+ visit did in April 2026, enriches courses for every student in the building.</li>
      <li><strong>Community projects through PUC.</strong> Projects with Underserved Communities teams co-design water access, sanitation, cookstoves, health clinics and community learning centers with the communities that will run them.</li>
      <li><strong>International students and scholars.</strong> A welcoming, well-resourced community for students and visiting scholars who come to the School from around the world.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

